# Project hero layout (locked)

Every project case study uses the **same hero + intro as `OGCR.html`**. Do not invent a new composition per project. Only swap content and assets.

## Required structure (in this order)

1. `section.project-hero` — one full-width image (`.project-image`)
2. `section.project-intro`
   - **Left** `.project-intro-left`: `h1.project-title` + `ul.project-tags` (tags sit at the bottom of the column)
   - **Right** `.project-intro-body`: `p.project-text` (project caption) + `dl.project-meta` in a 2×2 grid

## Meta fields (never rename or reorder)

- Client
- With
- Role
- Year

## Do not

- Move tags, caption, or meta into a different column
- Replace tags with a metadata list (Year/Location/Team/Type, etc.)
- Add overlays, extra credits blocks, or a different intro grid
- Restyle this block with project-specific CSS

Reuse existing classes only (`project-hero`, `project-intro`, `project-tags`, `project-meta`). Navbar, footer, and the rest of the case study can differ; this hero/intro cannot.
